Subject: [PATCH 2/4] N_V v2 estimator: c_i = w_i/((t+h_i) rho(h_i,t)), sigma
 terms differentiated through rho (tier 1, Gate D; v2 registration 2026-10-15;
 Core only, no UI, nothing wired in)

Tests first: on a stub (rho = 1) 6 of 12 red (rho hand values, quadrature cross-check, 3-object value, T1 value, sigma hand terms, synthetic-foil fixture); the rho(0,t)=1 test and both finite-difference tests pass on the stub (v1 is self-consistent) and are broken by mutation instead. Green: 12/12 PrecipitateNumberDensityTests. rho by composite Simpson in theta (q = sin theta), node count growing with h/t; tests compare it with the closed form, a theta trapezoid and a q midpoint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
